WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.009
Hey David, how do we move the Republican party
to the left?

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:08.610
It's a good question and there are basically
two answers.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.590
Number one is we moved the Republican party
to the left by moving the democratic parties

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.590
that at off.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:19.050
The second answer is we move the Republican
party to the left by working at the local

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.810
level like Republicans are so good at doing
to get left wingers elected to school boards

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:32.550
and city councils and PTA, you know, whatever
at the local level because this is how Republicans

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.319
have successfully won thousands of seats.

00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:40.429
If you consider down to the local level, tens
of thousands of seats even, excuse me, over

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:43.399
the last several years, several decades actually.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:49.729
Number one, if we can move the Overton window
to the left of national political discussions,

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:52.570
the Republican party is going to have to come
left at least on some issues.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.740
A lot of them have on the issue of gay marriage,
for example.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.999
It feels like so long ago, but it wasn't that
long ago that the Supreme court decision in

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:06.060
June of 2015 said you can't ban same sex marriage
at the state level and not all, there's still

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:11.289
a lot of money raised in evangelical circles
around being anti-gay, but a lot of Republicans

00:01:11.289 --> 00:01:15.940
have just sort of forgotten about it and they're
now at least centrists on the issue of gay

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.940
marriage.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.079
It's just one example.

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:22.060
As we continue to move the conversation to
the left on health care, the catalyst for

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.789
which was Bernie Sanders back in 2016 inserting
this issue, uh, in a serious way into the

00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:33.219
public discussion overall, you are pulling
Republicans to the left as well.

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:37.869
Now they still want free market, blah, blah,
blah, all of that stuff.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:42.600
But more of them are willing to make some
concessions about either preexisting conditions

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.600
or whatever else.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:49.009
So the point is if the democratic party moves
to the left, it will force because we know

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:51.420
that the public is moving left as well.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.740
It will force the Republican party to come
somewhat to the left.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.240
And then we've got to work at the local level.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.409
I know that it's, it sounds so boring.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.170
It sounds almost cliche.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:06.280
Uh, it sounds almost axiomatic to say Democrats
have to be working at the local level, but

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.920
Democrats just don't do it.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.360
Well, the Democrats don't do it well.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.860
That's the reality and what happens is there's
a sort of two fold effect, number one by working

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.080
really well at the local level, everything
from school boards to city councils, to mayor,

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.959
ships of smaller towns and cities, all that
stuff.

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:29.959
Uh, what Republicans do is they make it so
that they aren't in a position to have to

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:34.870
make things happen at the state or federal
level as quickly because they have all these

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.900
people already doing it when it comes to curricula
in schools because they've got the school

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.750
boards, all of these other things.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:48.580
If we can get involved in that, we are going
to have a lot of those same successes presumably.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.250
But also they have basically like a farm team
to use a baseball analogy.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.310
They've got the minor leagues and they have
all sorts of people from which they can hand

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:02.379
pick the most charismatic and the most sort
of PR friendly and then start winning bigger

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:04.230
races in the house of representatives.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.340
Some of these folks can even become senators,
et cetera.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.120
So those are the two areas where Democrats
need to start working right away.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.730
If we want to move the Republican party to
the left, we know the way to do it.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:19.620
Move ourselves to the left as leftists, both
through the democratic party and outside of

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:20.620
it.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.989
Uh, and we've got to start winning the local
races.

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:27.530
It's just, it's, it's truly disheartening
to see the degree to which Democrats have

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:33.479
failed at the local level for so many years
and in large swaths of the United States.

